    "source_notes": [
      "Migrated from the legacy proprietary FUD70S/FUD71 profile to Registry v3.",
      "The manufacturer documentation confirms bidirectional operation and status feedback: ORG 0x05 sends one PTM200-style byte with DB3=0x70 for on and DB3=0x50 for off; ORG 0x07 sends a 4BS status telegram with DB3=0x02, DB2=dimming value in percent, DB1=0x00 and DB0=0x08/0x09 for off/on.",
      "The physical actuator receives control telegrams from a corresponding A5-38-08 controller profile. TX messages are intentionally not duplicated in this proprietary profile; runtime resolves them through config/device-controller-mappings.json.",
      "Profile is intentionally bidirectional at device level, although this registry file only contains proprietary RX telegram definitions.",
